Revision history for WWW-MetaForge

{{$NEXT}}

 - Add the Pendola Pass map (pendola-pass) to maps and map_display_names
 - Item: expose the API's used_in list, the items this item is a component of
 - Declare LWP::Protocol::https as a prerequisite; the API is HTTPS-only, so
   without it a fresh install died with "LWP::Protocol::https not installed"
   on the first request
 - Align the ARC Raiders result classes with the current live API response
   format; this changes which attributes are available and may be
   incompatible for code reading result fields:
   - Item: item_type, value, stat_block
   - Arc: simplified fields
   - Quest: nested rewards, trader_name, xp
   - Trader: inventory item fields
 - Add the riven-tides and stella-montis maps
 - Add the CLI subcommands `map <map-id>` (GameMapData markers, --type filter)
   and `trader <name>` (single-trader inventory)
 - Realign the Quest and Arc CLI commands with the live API; output of fields
   the API never sent is dropped
 - Add Result::Arc attribute `loot` (the CLI requests includeLoot=true) and
   Result::Quest attribute `guide_url`; `guide_links` is dead upstream
 - Fix the CLI item lookup not sending includeComponents, which left the
   crafting, sold-by and recycle sections empty
 - Fix Result::Quest::from_hashref reading camelCase keys the API does not
   send
 - The pagination stops after 100 pages and dies with an error instead of
   returning an incomplete answer
 - An API error names the method and the path of the request
 - The README names the cache directory and the maps that the code uses
 - The prerequisites name the distributions they come from: Types::Standard,
   which the type constraints need, and HTTP::Message, which ships
   HTTP::Request and HTTP::Response, so a fresh install loads the library
   instead of failing on a missing module; t/cpanfile.t holds the list
 - map_data uses the user agent given to WWW::MetaForge::ArcRaiders, so an
   injected user agent also serves the map requests
 - Items expose recycle_from, dropped_by, mods, locations, cosmetic,
   relationships, guide_links, guide_url, flavor_text, subcategory,
   ammo_type, shield_type, loot_area, article, unlocks_weapon and
   created_at
 - `metaforge-arcraiders item` shows what an item is used in, what recycles
   into it, which ARCs drop it, compatible mods or weapons, map locations,
   cosmetic options and guide links
 - `metaforge-arcraiders items --category` and `--rarity` filter on the
   server across all pages, matching the exact API value
 - Arc: add `data` with the ARC's variants; `metaforge-arcraiders arcs
   --loot` requests includeLoot=true; `metaforge-arcraiders arc` shows
   whether an ARC flies and the rarity of each drop
 - Quest: add `description`, `additional_rewards` and `manifest`;
   `metaforge-arcraiders quest` shows the trader, prerequisites,
   description, required and granted items by name and quantity, and all
   rewards
 - Add Result::Ermal and the `ermal` method for Ermal's offers and permanent
   services from the traders response, and the CLI command
   `metaforge-arcraiders ermal`
 - Map markers: add `community`, `source_id` and `route_id`; `lootAreas` is
   typed as a string; `metaforge-arcraiders map` flags community markers
 - Event timers follow the events-schedule format: Result::EventTimer and
   its TimeSlot read only the epoch-millisecond records of /events-schedule;
   next_time returns undef when no slot of the schedule window lies ahead;
   with region => 'all' the timers are grouped per region and carry the new
   attribute region
 - event_timers_cached and event_timers_raw keep the cached events schedule
   until a timer that had a run ahead when it was fetched starts its last
   one, then fetch it again, so a cached timer's next_time does not run out
   while the API knows later runs; a TTL for event_timers still applies
 - The event_timers documentation lists the query parameters the live API
   accepts (region, map, name)
 - The event command shows the date of every slot, takes map IDs for --map
   and names the maps an event runs on when the given map does not match
 - Add the hideout: ->hideout returns each hideout station with what its
   upgrade levels take, and the "hideout" command lists the stations or
   shows one level by level
 - Add the weekly trials: ->weekly_trials returns the running, upcoming and
   catalog trials and ->weekly_trials_window the window times; the "trials"
   command shows them. A cached answer is kept only until the trial window
   changes
 - Name MetaForge ARC Raiders (https://metaforge.app/arc-raiders) as the
   data source in the README and in the POD of WWW::MetaForge,
   WWW::MetaForge::GameMapData and metaforge-arcraiders, and list the newer
   ARC Raiders data and commands there
 - Add an opt-in live API test (t/50-live-api.t, WWW_METAFORGE_USE_LIVE_API=1)
   that checks every covered endpoint and flags response keys missing from
   the fixtures
 - Fix the CLI output encoding: --json printed UTF-8 encoded twice, and
   text run from Perl (new_with_cmd) printed Latin-1 bytes or warned
   "Wide character"; every command now prints UTF-8 encoded exactly once
 - Fix the cache writing its JSON files UTF-8 encoded twice; they are now
   encoded once and the file name carries the format version
   (<endpoint>_<md5>.v2.json), so files of the old format are no longer read
   and are fetched again, and clear removes both
 - Add Cache get_entry, the stored entry with its timestamp, ignoring the
   TTL; event_timers_hourly uses it instead of reading the cache file itself
 - Fix the CLI not decoding its arguments: `quest "Celeste’s Journals"` found
   nothing and echoed the name double encoded; arguments and option values are
   now decoded from UTF-8, and an argument that is not UTF-8 is an error
 - `--json` output has sorted keys in every command
 - Fix metaforge-arcraiders documenting SUPPORT twice: its Discord, IRC and
   repository links are under COMMUNITY, SUPPORT is generated once
 - Fix the POD and the usage messages of the commands naming the program
   arcraiders: they name metaforge-arcraiders, the name it is installed under

0.002     2026-01-11 04:45:55Z

 - Convert POD documentation to @Author::GETTY inline style

0.001     2026-01-05 05:03:59Z

 - Initial release
 - ARC Raiders API client (items, quests, traders, arcs, events, map data)
 - CLI tool: metaforge-arcraiders
 - Response caching with configurable TTL
